{"version":"v4.16","date":"9 November 2026","iso":"2026-11-09","preamble":{"paras":["We, the peoples of the Balkan Confederation, and all the communities who share this land,","United by one language of a thousand faces which, from place to place, makes us mutually intelligible from the Julian Alps to the shores of the Black Sea, and holding this mutual understanding, older than our borders and our quarrels, as the first of our common goods;","Aware that we inhabit the one crossroads of Europe where the Latin West, the Byzantine East and the Ottoman world met, overlapped and mingled on the same soil, and recognising this overlap, long lived as a rupture, as our singularity;","Having each, in our turn and under different masters, known the subjection of empires, and knowing from an experience paid for in blood that no people is free while it dominates another;","Having each, in our turn, set the same refusal against empires, and built our nations not against empires alone, but against the very idea that one people may govern another without its consent;","Remembering those among us who made war on one another, and refusing both the oblivion that betrays the dead and the rancour that condemns the living;","Resolved to found our union neither on blood, nor on a supposed common origin, nor on the domination of the most numerous, but solely on the freely renewed will to live together;","Affirming that this Confederation is not one more empire, but its exact opposite: a home one enters by choice, remains in by consent, and that no one is compelled to inhabit;","Determined to guarantee to everyone their language, their faith, their memory and their letters, and to every person the right to belong to no one but themselves;","We give ourselves this Constitution."],"motto":"Naš dom — Our home."},"titles":[{"id":"title-1","num":"Title I","name":"General provisions","arts":[["art-1","Article 1","The Balkan Confederation"],["art-2","Article 2","Purpose"],["art-3","Article 3","Th